# Binaries
bin/
# The TypeScript package's dist IS committed (a git install has no
# toolchain); its node_modules is not.
ts/node_modules/
# `go build ./cmd/<name>` drops the binary here, named for the command.
/acceptance
# ko / goreleaser output; NOT the web console — frontend/dist is COMMITTED
# (the embed needs it and `go build` must work without a Node toolchain).
/dist/
!frontend/dist/

# TypeScript's incremental-build cache. NOT committed: `tsc -b` rewrites
# it on every build, so a tracked copy makes every build dirty the working
# tree -- which CI reads as "the recipe modified the tree" and fails,
# correctly. It carries no information anybody else needs; the artifact
# that matters is frontend/dist, above.
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

